<title>PANAMA: Panama to privatize state phone INTEL next month.</title>
<headline>Panama to privatize state phone INTEL next month.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama intends to sell off 49 percent of state phone company INTEL next month, Planning and Economic Policy Minister Guillermo Chapman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will set a date next week on the public bid which should take place next month,&quot; he told the Foreign Press Association.</p>
<p>Cable and Wireless Plc and GTE Corp are the only companies that have qualified to bid. INTEL is said to be worth some $2 billion in total.</p>
<p>((-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739))</p>
